{
 "_source": "Live plant, 2026-11-20, local time (UTC+2): one SCS bus with an F461 2.0.11 and an F455 1.0.76, one Home Assistant instance per gateway, and an F418 dimmer at WHERE 0010. Each trace is the WHO 1 frames of that dimmer in one instance's debug log: tx a frame the instance sent (logged when the gateway acknowledged it), rx a frame it received on its event session or as a reply. No address, MAC or name of the plant.",
 "_traces": {
  "f455_on_at_level_0": "F455 Home Assistant instance. The dimmer was off with a remembered level of 0 (how it got there is not known). `light.turn_on` for six lights: the dimmer reports on (`*1*1*0010##`, `*1*2*0010##`) and answers the level read with level 0 in DIMENSION 1. Twelve seconds later another client's status request is answered `*1*2*0010##`: it is still on.",
  "f461_on_at_level_0": "The F461 Home Assistant instance during the same seconds (it sent nothing; `*1*1000#1*0010##` is the F461's report of the command on the bus).",
  "f461_levels": "F461 Home Assistant instance, forty minutes later, the dimmer still remembering level 0. Another client reads the status and the level every few seconds. Off: `*1*0*0010##` and DIMENSION 4 level 0. On: `*1*2*0010##` and DIMENSION 1 level 0, three reads in 12 s. Then the level is written to 1, 2, 5, 10 and 20 % (`*#1*0010*#1*101*0##` ...): DIMENSION 1 reports each, the status goes 2, 2, 2, 3, 4. Off, and on again: back at 20 %.",
  "f461_dim_steps": "Same instance. Dim-down steps (`*1*31*0010##`, sent by another client) from 20 %: 8 %, then 1 %, and it stays at 1 % (`*#1*0010*1*101*10##`) however many more follow: the steps do not reach level 0. Off and on: 1 %. Two steps up: 8 %, 16 %.",
  "f461_level_0_write_through_f455": "Same instance. Another client writes level 0 (`*#1*0010*#1*100*0##`) through the F455, which acknowledges it (the F461 refused the same frame a moment before): the dimmer goes to 1 % and stays on. It is not what leaves a dimmer at level 0.",
  "f461_off_with_speed": "Same instance. On at 60 %, then off with a speed (`*1*0#2*0010##`, another client): off, DIMENSION 4 level 0, and a plain on brings it back at 60 %."
 },
